  "correction": "Existing approved Chrome/Electron ZIP paths retain exact managed-vault artifact admission, original context, current owned project/source, egress policy and one-use authority. Desktop release now uses the same canonical confirmation architecture, producer proof, current GitHub connection, owned project/repository, immutable commit and exact workflow bytes before one lightweight tag create. Its actual ref receipt and readback must match. There is no annotated-tag or alternate workflow/branch dispatch fallback. Polling requires the exact tag and commit, validates current tag before and after release metadata, owner/credential/cancellation and canonical GitHub asset URLs, rejects credential-bearing projections and never selects latest. Network, stream and JSON diagnostics are sanitized.",
  "limitations": [
